{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/pushwooshcore\/pwconfiguration\/resetuserid"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"+ (","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:v","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"void"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resetUserId","kind":"identifier"},{"text":";","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["iOS"],"languages":["occ"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this on logout or account deletion. The user ID becomes the HWID again, as on a fresh install,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and the SDK sends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/registerUser"},{"type":"text","text":" with the HWID so the server stops attributing the device to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"previous user. ","type":"text"},{"code":"setUserId(\"\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does not reset the user: an empty value is ignored."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The call waits until the SDK is ready, like ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setUserId:"},{"type":"text","text":". If the HWID was already registered"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the user less than a day ago, no request is sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Example","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func handleLogout() {","    Pushwoosh.configure.resetUserId()","    Pushwoosh.configure.setTags([\"logged_in\": false])","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"code":["[[Pushwoosh configure] resetUserId];"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"objc"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Resets the user identifier to the HWID."}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"text","text":"+ "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"resetUserId"}],"roleHeading":"Type Method","symbolKind":"method","role":"symb